Game Stream for Ubuntu amd64
===========================

Install with:
  sudo apt install ./game-stream_0.2.0_amd64.deb

Open Applications > Game Stream. First launch requires internet and about 2 GB
of free disk space for its private Python dependencies and Chromium browser.
A progress dialog reports setup. Native system dependencies are installed by
apt; no Python packages or browsers are downloaded by root maintainer scripts.
The per-user runtime is under ~/.local/share/game-stream (or XDG_DATA_HOME).
If interrupted, launch again. A previous working runtime is kept if an update
fails. Setup diagnostics are in ~/.local/state/game-stream/setup.log.

Close the app before uninstalling. Run as the normal desktop user:
  game-stream-uninstall
Optional removal of this user's preferences/session/catalog:
  game-stream-uninstall --purge-user-data
Dry run:
  game-stream-uninstall --dry-run

Or remove only the system package:
  sudo apt remove game-stream
This preserves user runtime/settings; the uninstall helper removes the owned
runtime too. Never run the application itself with sudo.

Ubuntu 22.04/24.04/26.04 amd64 with Python 3.10-3.15 is the intended target.
Other desktop Linux distributions can use the documented source installation.
This is not an Android APK and does not run on Android.
